# Keep the setup section current

The README has a section **"Setting it up on another computer"**. Whenever a change affects how someone
installs or sets up Stems Studio, update that section in the same commit and refresh its "Last checked" date:

- prerequisites (Git, Python, browser, GPU), `Install.bat` / `Install.command` steps, optional installs
- new files or settings a new computer needs (for example `settings.json` / `STEMS_STUDIO_LIBRARY`)
- changes to where the library lives or how song folders are named
- the update check, or anything that makes versions on different computers incompatible
- model downloads or other first-run steps

Say honestly what has and has not been tested (clean machine, Mac).
